// Cognitive Workspace completion matrix: what "the program is done" means, row by row.
//
// Read by config/scripts/check-cognitive-workspace-completeness.mjs. `--integrity` (PR-safe) checks the
// matrix is well-formed and every pointer resolves; the default mode is the program done-gate and is
// red while any row is open. A row may be `complete` only on evidence that resolves — never on an
// artifact merely existing. It COMPOSES config/reliability-gates.jsonc (a row may cite a gate id)
// rather than duplicating it. Blocked is narrow: only an Owner authorization or runner capacity.
// Residual trust: a complete row pointing at an unrelated passing gate is a review question.
